Hi,

I've modified Proll so that it can be used in a ROM, which is needed for 
QEMU. All stuff in .data are moved to either .text or .bss.

The patch adds a directory for QEMU-specific files, which are basically 
MrCoffee ones but just unnecessary stuff thrown out.

The new font file is preprocessed so that no bit twisting is needed at 
startup. This and some of the other modifications should be useful for other 
setups as well.

Do any of you linux gurus feel that Qemu emulating Sun4m could be useful for 
your kernel debugging businesses?

